FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:639 — closed-surface matrix skips when `member_resolves(module, builtin)` is true, but that predicate is derived from `MODULE_MEMBERS` itself, so an over-permissive table hides the exact case it should catch; guard at tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:700 (`checked > BUILTIN_NAMES.len()`) only fails if the table grants nearly everything — why it matters: e.g. adding `uppercase` under `csv` makes `csv.uppercase` answer while the matrix skips it and stays green (only the three hardcoded rows in `edge_a_module_does_not_answer` would catch their three pairs) — concrete fix: derive the skip-allow from an independent allowlist (documents or hardcoded SPEC promises), not from the table under test, and enumerate the refusal universe from short member names.
2. [MAJOR] src/stdlib.rs:74 — `length` listed under `list` (and src/stdlib.rs:102 under `text`) is undocumented dotted surface contradicting SPEC.md:1009 (`a module has the functions that are spelled <module>_<member> in the registry`, no `list_length`/`text_length` in src/stdlib.rs:749) — SPEC.md:1035 documents `text` with only `uppercase/lowercase/split/join` and SPEC.md:1042 writes `length` flat, README.md:237 and README.md:253 write `length` flat, SPEC.md:1104 lists only `list.map` — why it matters: phase enshrines new answering spellings (`say text.length` pinned at tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:1380) without documenting them, the drift direction it was to remove, and no reverse table=>documented gate exists (tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:596 only checks documented=>in-table) — concrete fix: document `text.length`/`list.length` in SPEC.md/README.md or remove them from `MODULE_MEMBERS` and the resolver.
3. [MAJOR] tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:638 — matrix walks `BUILTIN_NAMES` which holds qualified names like `files_read`/`json_parse` (src/stdlib.rs:787), so short suffixes (`read`/`parse`/`get`) as members of other modules (`json.read`, `text.get`, `files.parse`) are never enumerated — why it matters: unlisted pairs that must be refused have a test on neither side; a resolver regression allowing any suffix stays green — concrete fix: enumerate `(module, short-member)` from `MODULE_MEMBERS` short names plus flat builtins instead of `BUILTIN_NAMES`.
4. [MINOR] src/interpreter.rs:2101 — qualified builtins bypass the table (`get_var(&qualified).is_none() && !answered_by_builtin`, comment at src/interpreter.rs:2097 says answerable `whether or not the table holds`, same at src/bytecode/vm.rs:2753) contradicting src/stdlib.rs:115 doc that `module_has_member` is `the predicate both engines resolve a dotted call against` — why it matters: claimed invariant `table is the enforced surface` is false for the qualified path; a future qualified addition answers with no table entry — concrete fix: check `module_has_member` before the `get_var` hit for dotted receivers, or correct the docs/REPORT to state the qualified path is registry-driven.
5. [MINOR] tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:156 — heading join-word skip `word != "and"` is case-sensitive while `module_spelling` at tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:184 folds case-insensitively, so `### JSON AND CSV` inserts documented module `AND` — why it matters: confusing `AND not in MODULES` failure on prose capitalisation — concrete fix: use `!word.eq_ignore_ascii_case("and")`.
